This function is already minimal, so the gain is likely small. The change caches `type` in a local and adds branch-prediction hints (`__builtin_expect`) for the common case, where the field's own type is already set. Behavior is unchanged: the same checks run in the same order and return the same values.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 t = type;
    if (__builtin_expect(t != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1))
        return t;

    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return p->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```